Provenance for sharp.jinja
=========================

This is a vendored, pinned copy of the Qwen3.8 "sharp" chat template from
the PieBru Strix-Halo/gfx1151 deployment repo. It is kept byte-identical to
the upstream file so its SHA-256 is reproducible.

Upstream URL (fetched 2026-08-27):
  https://github.com/PieBru/Qwen-3.8-27B_Strix-Halo_gfx1151/blob/main/models/sharp.jinja

Upstream repository:
  https://github.com/PieBru/Qwen-3.8-27B_Strix-Halo_gfx1151
  (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 PieBru <piebru@gmail.com>)

Template version (line 1 of the file):
  qwen3.8-froggeric-v22.3

SHA-256 of this vendored file (verify with `sha256sum sharp.jinja`):
  6e1439c913ad7df4a966493ad70de7e7fc5a548d41bbe417c1571f766603629b

Why this template
-----------------
The Qwen3.8-27B GGUF embedded chat template does not correctly round-trip
OpenAI-compatible tool calls (see PieBru issue tracker and
ggml-org/llama.cpp issue #27588: trailing `assistant(tool_calls)` is silently
dropped in the auto-prefill/continuation path). `sharp.jinja` is a reviewed,
tested replacement that handles tool calls (default `tool_call_format = xml`),
the `enable_thinking` / `preserve_thinking` / `preserve_reasoning` kwargs,
and reasoning-effort steering. It is loaded with `--jinja --chat-template
<path>`.

Re-pinning
----------
To re-pin to a newer upstream version, fetch the new file, record its new
SHA-256 here, and re-run the tool-call fixtures (see
doc/qwen38-gfx1151/ and tests/qwen38-toolcall/). Do NOT ship a template
change based only on a successful model load.
